Strategy Guidance:
Design your algorithm to maintain a population of candidate solutions. At each step, balance exploration (probing new regions of the search space) and exploitation (refining the most promising solutions found so far).

Before writing code, reason through:
1. How will you balance global exploration of the search space with fine-grained local exploitation around the best basin of attraction?
2. How should step sizes or mutation radii adapt over iterations as the evaluation budget is consumed?
